\ Synthetic wide year candidates far beyond the signed 32-bit axis.
\ Opening and closing coordinates differ by 2070 days, with six
\ distinct gate spans. This is a valid physically possible year.
\ Its coordinates and gate indices are themselves 49-digit values.
\ These tests do not invoke any full sauce or gate traversal.

The wide year test magnitude is a wide quantity.
The wide year test day is a wide signed day.

To prepare the synthetic immense wide year:
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's opening day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000002070" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000001000000" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's opening index from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000001000006" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing index from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the first wide candidate.

To check enormous wide year containment:
  Prepare the synthetic immense wide year.
  If the first wide candidate's valid is not 1,
    put "The immense but short year candidate was rejected." into the check report; exit.
  If the first wide candidate's year length is not "2070",
    put "The immense wide year day length was wrong." into the check report; exit.
  If the first wide candidate's span count is not "6",
    put "The immense wide year gate-span count was wrong." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the wide year test day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  If the first wide candidate contains the wide year test day,
    put "An immense year included its opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000001" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the wide year test day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  If the first wide candidate does not contain the wide year test day,
    put "An immense year excluded the day after its opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000002070" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the wide year test day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  If the first wide candidate does not contain the wide year test day,
    put "An immense year excluded its closing gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000002071" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the wide year test day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  If the first wide candidate contains the wide year test day,
    put "An immense year included the day after its closing gate." into the check report; exit.

To check enormous wide year ordering:
  Prepare the synthetic immense wide year.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000010" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the second wide candidate's opening day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000002080" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the second wide candidate's closing day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000001000010" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the second wide candidate's opening index from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000001000016" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the second wide candidate's closing index from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the second wide candidate.
  If the second wide candidate's valid is not 1,
    put "The competing wide year was unexpectedly invalid." into the check report; exit.
  If the first wide candidate does not come before the second wide candidate,
    put "Equal-length wide years did not sort by earlier opening." into the check report; exit.
  If the second wide candidate comes before the first wide candidate,
    put "The wide year tie-breaker was not antisymmetric." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000001810" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the second wide candidate's closing day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the second wide candidate.
  If the second wide candidate does not come before the first wide candidate,
    put "A shorter wide year did not precede a longer one." into the check report; exit.

To check invalid wide year endpoints:
  Prepare the synthetic immense wide year.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000001000005" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing index from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the first wide candidate.
  If the first wide candidate's valid is not 0,
    put "A wide year containing fewer than six gaps was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000001000100" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing index from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the first wide candidate.
  If the first wide candidate's valid is not 0,
    put "Wide year length ignored the 42-day minimum per gap." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000001000006" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing index from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the first wide candidate.
  If the first wide candidate's valid is not 0,
    put "A zero-duration wide year candidate was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Prepare the synthetic immense wide year.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000250" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the first wide candidate.
  If the first wide candidate's valid is not 0,
    put "A wide year shorter than 252 days was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Prepare the synthetic immense wide year.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000005779" into the wide year test magnitude.
  Set the first wide candidate's closing day from the wide year test magnitude given 1.
  Measure the first wide candidate.
  If the first wide candidate's valid is not 0,
    put "A wide year longer than 5778 days was accepted." into the check report; exit.
